<svelte:head><title>Review, versions & sharing · Review Room</title><meta name="description" content="Review a take, leave feedback, choose the current version and share with the right audience." /></svelte:head>
<header class="docs-heading"><p class="docs-kicker">Using Review Room</p><h1>Watch the take.<br />Make the decision clear.</h1><p class="docs-lead">A version, a review decision and permission to publish answer different questions. Check each one before sending work onward.</p></header>
<figure class="docs-visual"><div class="docs-annotated"><img class="docs-screenshot" src="/docs/images/review-workspace-20261024.png" width="2035" height="1060" alt="Owner workspace: version menu above the player, review decisions below it, and Notes panel on the right." /><span class="docs-pin pin-version" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="docs-pin pin-decision" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="docs-pin pin-notes" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div><div class="docs-callouts"><p><strong>1 · Choose a version</strong>The menu above the player chooses the take you inspect.</p><p><strong>2 · Record a decision</strong>Shortlist, stars and approval sit below the player.</p><p><strong>3 · Add context</strong>Notes holds feedback. Fields holds the selected version’s creative metadata.</p></div><figcaption>Owner workspace, verified October 24, 2026. Private reviewers have fewer controls. On smaller screens, secondary tools move below or behind a toggle.</figcaption></figure>
<section id="feedback"><h2>Leave feedback that can be acted on</h2><ol class="docs-steps"><li>Open an asset and check the selected version. For video, pause at the moment you want to discuss.</li><li>Open <strong>Notes & info</strong>, choose <strong>Notes</strong>, and type your feedback. Keep the timecode checked to attach that moment, or uncheck it for a general note.</li><li>Use <strong>Add note</strong> to save. Wait for it to appear in the note list; a draft is not a saved comment.</li><li>Use <strong>Request changes</strong> or <strong>Approve</strong> for the review outcome. Rate or shortlist independently. The owner can follow outstanding notes in the feedback inbox and mark handled feedback complete.</li></ol><p>On still images, expand the preview to draw markup, undo local strokes, clear or save it. Saved markup is separate from the original image file.</p><aside class="docs-note"><strong>Comments belong to the asset.</strong><p>The current model does not pin comments to an exact take. Include the version label in the note when it matters, especially for timecoded feedback read after the current take changes.</p></aside></section>
<section id="versions"><h2>Inspecting a take and making it current</h2><p>The <strong>Asset version</strong> menu above the player offers the current/latest view and stored versions. Selecting an older take lets you inspect it. When the selected take differs from the saved pick, <strong>Make current</strong> chooses it as the asset’s current take. This preserves the other versions.</p><p>Open <strong>Fields</strong> to check the selected version’s prompt, model, notes and reference images before using <strong>Save version metadata</strong>. Missing data stays empty. If another session saved first, a conflict retains the draft; reload and reconcile before saving again.</p><p>For an existing video publication, <strong>Publish & share → Video embeds → New version</strong> uploads a revision to that same asset. Creative Studio Pro can also add takes by production code through the scoped API; manual drops into its locked folders follow the filename-matching rules in the naming guide. A separate ordinary upload creates a separate asset.</p><p>Approval, rating and shortlist describe the asset. Prompt, model and image references describe the exact version. Making a take current does not publish it or replace an already published take.</p></section>
<section id="private-review"><h2>Invite someone to a private review</h2><ol class="docs-steps"><li>The owner opens <strong>Publish & share → Private review</strong>.</li><li>Choose the intended project, optional passcode, expiry and download permission, then use <strong>Create private link</strong>. Copy the resulting link for the intended reviewers. This control creates project-wide links.</li><li>The reviewer opens the link and completes its access prompt. They can watch, leave notes, rate, shortlist and make supported review decisions. Downloads require both link permission and enabled asset downloads.</li><li>To withdraw access, use <strong>Revoke</strong>. An expired, revoked or unavailable link cannot be used as a public embed or a permanent media URL.</li></ol><p>Private review links do not grant folder management, project archive or production deletion controls. An owner session and a private review session are different access paths.</p></section>
<section id="publication"><h2>Publish selected versions to Trailer Feed</h2><p>Use <strong>Publish & share</strong> to connect an ordinary project or folder to Trailer Feed. Confirm the exact ready video versions. <strong>Publish all videos</strong> is a one-time selection; <strong>Choose versions</strong> lets the owner select individual takes. Review the included grid/reference images before confirming. Publication consent is explicit and does not require an additional approval-status gate.</p><p>A new source upload remains private and does not silently replace published work. Trailer Feed assigns its own project-local version numbers in the selected versions’ creation order, oldest first. Source asset codes and source version IDs remain the stable integration identity.</p><div class="docs-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Refresh metadata</td><td>Fills available empty target fields. Preserves deliberate Trailer Feed edits and existing media URLs. Newly included images require explicit consent.</td></tr><tr><td>Unsync</td><td>Withdraws that delivery. Source media and feedback remain in Review Room; retries must not resurrect the removed entry.</td></tr><tr><td>Sync again</td><td>Requires fresh confirmation after disconnection. It is separate from retrying a failed delivery.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Creative Studio Pro’s locked folders cannot connect directly. Use <strong>Copy to folder</strong> to place selected deliverables in an ordinary folder, then connect that folder. The copy has its own asset identity and shares the stored bytes.</p></section>
<figure class="docs-visual docs-sharing-figure"><img class="docs-screenshot" src="/docs/images/private-sharing-20261024.png" alt="Private review tab in Publish & share, showing the project, optional passcode, expiry and two separate download permissions." width="480" height="650" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Private review controls.</strong> Select the project first. Passcode and expiry restrict the link. Downloads need both “Allow enabled asset downloads” on the link and permission for the asset’s original. Creating a private link does not publish a video to Trailer Feed.</figcaption></figure>
<section id="embeds"><h2>Video embeds and showcases</h2><p><strong>Video embeds</strong> is a separate publication path for approved, ready video versions and exact allowed HTTPS site origins. <strong>Replace at URL</strong> updates an existing embed to an eligible replacement version while keeping its slug. <strong>Revoke</strong> disables it. An ordered <strong>Showcase</strong> combines existing published videos in a chosen order. These controls are distinct from private review and Trailer Feed destination sync.</p></section>
